[claude:event result] {"duration_api_ms":79553,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f13b50f4-75a6-454e-8f90-fbecddb91dac","total_cost_usd":0.0699834,"usage":{"input_tokens":73,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9350,"cache_read_input_tokens":169589,"output_tokens":8032,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5001},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9350},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":8,"output_tokens":469,"cache_read_input_tokens":22003,"cache_creation_input_tokens":190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":190,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1024,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.001104,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-haiku-4-5":{"inputTokens":73,"outputTokens":8032,"cacheReadInputTokens":169589,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9350,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.06887940000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":5001,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":9,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Done! I've created the `run_tasks` function in `/app/run.py` with the following features:\n\n**Implementation details:**\n- Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to enforce the `max_concurrent` limit\n- Wraps each task callable so it acquires the semaphore before running\n- On `KeyboardInterrupt`: cancels tasks that haven't started yet, then waits for all running tasks to complete (allowing their cleanup code in finally blocks to run), then re-raises the interrupt\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Tasks are created upfront with `asyncio.create_task()`\n2. First `gather()` runs them with concurrency control via semaphore\n3. If `KeyboardInterrupt` occurs, any pending tasks are cancelled\n4. Second `gather()` waits for all tasks to finish (currently running ones complete with cleanup)\n5. The interrupt is re-raised\n\nThe tests confirm it correctly limits concurrency to 3 tasks, runs cleanup code even when interrupted, and can be imported as `from run import run_tasks`.","ttft_ms":43346,"type":"result","duration_ms":79753,"uuid":"e775e6de-2267-4aac-9642-f63a727a9fcc","ttft_stream_ms":900,"time_to_request_ms":74,"queued_turn_count":0}
